// Signing lives here rather than in project.pbxproj, so that a public checkout
// carries no Apple Team ID and so cloning this repo doesn't mean editing the
// project file to build it.
//
// Put your own team in Local.xcconfig, next to this file. It is gitignored:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//
// To find yours:
//
//     security find-identity -v -p codesigning
//     security find-certificate -c "<the common name>" -p | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//
// The Team ID is the certificate's OU field. It is *not* the code in parentheses
// in the common name — that identifies the certificate, and using it here fails
// the build with a signing error that doesn't explain itself.
//
// Without Local.xcconfig the project still opens and builds for the simulator;
// only device builds and archiving fail, with "requires a development team".
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
